This project is a new Rust/macOS implementation informed by DriftWM's infinite
canvas design. It does not claim to compile or run the upstream Wayland/Smithay
compositor on macOS. Canvas algorithm adaptations and any copied source have
additional provenance in their source files. Most macOS platform integration is
new. The optional native/privileged/loader.m is adapted from yabai at commit
dd845723416f5fe92af49fad5ebab00369e07edd and retains its MIT license, copyright,
and Jeremy Legendre arm64e attribution. The exact upstream license is retained
in native/privileged/YABAI-LICENSE.txt.
native/desktop/window-events.m and the event handling of
native/desktop/window-manager.m are adapted from yabai at the same commit
(src/workspace.m, src/application.c, src/application.h, src/window.c,
src/window.h, src/event_loop.c, src/window_manager.c: which notifications an
application and a window are observed with, and what each one means), MIT,
Copyright (c) 2019 Åsmund Vikane. Its license text is retained in
native/families/YABAI-NOTICE.txt, which the app bundle carries beside this
file, and each adapted file names what it took.
native/focus/focus.m brings a window that is on another desktop forward with
the calls and the event record of yabai's window_manager_focus_window_with_raise
and window_manager_make_key_window (src/window_manager.c:1269-1335,
src/misc/extern.h:81-82, src/window_manager.h:5) at the same commit, under the
same license and copyright.
crates/core carries DriftWM's pure modules (canvas, config, layout, session,
stage and the touch gesture recogniser) from the source baseline with their
tests; each file records its upstream path, and crates/core/PORT.md lists every
hash and deviation. Its stand-ins for Smithay geometry and input types follow
Smithay 0.7.0 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2017 Victor Berger and Victoria Brekenfeld),
and its key-name lookup reimplements libxkbcommon's rules (MIT/X11).
